# Exclusions for scripts/link.sh, applied hierarchically: this file governs
# the whole hub, and any .ignore in a subdirectory governs that directory
# and below. Syntax is gitignore-style; rules apply in order and the last
# match wins, so ! re-includes. Unlike git, ! can also re-include paths
# under an excluded directory.
#
#   scratch/         directory named scratch anywhere below this file
#   drafts/*.md      anchored here (the pattern contains a slash)
#   !drafts/keep.md  re-include one path
#   [claude] tmp/    scope a rule to one harness: claude or opencode
#   [claude,opencode] tmp/   scope a rule to several harnesses
#
# Nothing is ignored until you add a pattern below.
